1
00:00:03,052 --> 00:00:03,694
On the hill,

2
00:00:03,744 --> 00:00:06,866
it's blowing so hard that Mila's kite pulls like crazy!

3
00:00:06,916 --> 00:00:09,568
But where does all this pushing air come from?

4
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:12,287
At the beach in the afternoon,

5
00:00:12,337 --> 00:00:14,672
Mila's ribbon flies toward the land.

6
00:00:14,722 --> 00:00:16,395
Noah feels the burning hot

7
00:00:16,445 --> 00:00:17,985
sand and the cool water…

8
00:00:18,035 --> 00:00:19,028
is that a clue?

9
00:00:19,812 --> 00:00:21,326
Discovery mission!

10
00:00:23,842 --> 00:00:24,421
Mini mode!

11
00:00:24,471 --> 00:00:27,127
The Sun heats the land faster than the sea.

12
00:00:27,177 --> 00:00:30,336
Above it, the air warms up, gets lighter and rises,

13
00:00:30,386 --> 00:00:32,651
so less air is left near the ground.

14
00:00:33,430 --> 00:00:35,687
Above the sea, the cool air is more packed,

15
00:00:35,737 --> 00:00:38,530
so it slides toward the land to take the empty place…

16
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,602
and that's the wind!

17
00:00:39,652 --> 00:00:40,246
And up high,

18
00:00:40,296 --> 00:00:42,227
the cooled air goes back to the sea.

19
00:00:43,028 --> 00:00:46,119
Everywhere on Earth it's the same: more air,

20
00:00:46,169 --> 00:00:48,832
high pressure; less air, low pressure.

21
00:00:48,882 --> 00:00:51,523
So air always runs from more to less.

22
00:00:52,318 --> 00:00:53,033
But at night,

23
00:00:53,083 --> 00:00:55,094
the land cools faster than the sea…

24
00:00:55,144 --> 00:00:56,331
and everything flips!

25
00:00:56,381 --> 00:00:58,215
The ribbon flies toward the sea,

26
00:00:58,265 --> 00:00:59,796
carried by a gentler wind.

27
00:01:00,625 --> 00:01:02,071
And that's where the wind comes from.

28
00:01:04,139 --> 00:01:06,908
The Sun heats the air unevenly; warm air rises,

29
00:01:06,958 --> 00:01:09,117
and cool air rushes in: that's wind.

30
00:01:10,084 --> 00:01:10,969
With an adult:

31
00:01:11,019 --> 00:01:14,240
hold a thin strip of paper above a warm radiator.

32
00:01:14,290 --> 00:01:16,960
It flies upward, because warm air rises!

33
00:01:17,741 --> 00:01:19,423
And how do clouds form?

34
00:01:19,473 --> 00:01:20,979
The answer tomorrow.
